OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F319A1786576712
OL,3,CAstronomers reveal photos of glasses
OL,4,Cused to view eclipse in 1927
OL,6,FAstronomers have revealed photographs
OL,7,Fof glasses from 1927 used to view
OL,8,Feclipses, ahead of the best solar
OL,9,Feclipse in decades this evening.
OL,11,FMore than 90% of the sun will be
OL,12,Fobscured by the moon between 6.17pm
OL,13,Fand 8.06pm on Wednesday, the most it
OL,14,Fhas been blocked above UK skies since
OL,15,Fthe total eclipse in 1999.
OL,17,FOn Wednesday, images from the Royal
OL,18,FSociety showed "Eclipsia" glasses
OL,19,Fspecially designed for viewing
OL,20,Feclipses almost a hundred years ago.
OL,26,@zD@POUzD@YO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/9
